rent.global_position + offset, 0.2)\n\tcard_ui.drop_point_detector.monitoring = false\n\tEvents.card_aim_started.emit(card_ui)\n\n\nfunc exit() -> void:\n\tEvents.card_aim_ended.emit(card_ui)\n\n\nfunc on_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\t\n\tvar mouse_motion := event is InputEventMouseMotion\n\tvar mouse_at_bottom := card_ui.get_global_mouse_position().y > MOUSE_Y_SNAPBACK_THRESHOLD\n\t\n\tif (mouse_motion and mouse_at_bottom) or event.is_action_pressed(\"right_mouse\"):\n\t\ttransition_requested.emit(self, CardState.State.BASE)\n\telif event.is_action_released(\"left_mouse\") or event.is_action_pressed(\"left_mouse\"):\n\t\tget_viewport().set_input_as_handled()\n\t\ttransition_requested.emit(self, CardState.State.RELEASED)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 13. `/workspace/scenes/ui/hand.gd` (10 lines)\n\n```gdscript\nextends HBoxContainer\n\nconst CARD_UI_SCENE := preload(\"res://scenes/card_ui/card_ui.tscn\")\n\n\nfunc add_card(card_title: String) -> void:\n\tvar new_card_ui = CARD_UI_SCENE.instantiate()\n\tadd_child(new_card_ui)\n\tnew_card_ui.home_parent = self\n\tnew_card_ui.card_title = card_title\n```\n\n---\n\n### 14. `/workspace/global/events.gd` (24 lines)\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\n# Card-related events\nsignal card_drag_started(card_ui: CardUI)\nsignal card_drag_ended(card_ui: CardUI)\nsignal card_aim_started(card_ui: CardUI)\nsignal card_aim_ended(card_ui: CardUI)\nsignal card_played(card: Card)\nsignal card_tooltip_requested(card: Card)\nsignal tooltip_hide_requested\n\n# Player-related events\nsignal player_hand_drawn\nsignal player_hand_discarded\nsignal player_turn_ended\nsignal player_hit\nsignal player_died\n\n# Enemy-related events\nsignal enemy_action_completed(enemy: Enemy)\nsignal enemy_turn_ended\n\n# Battle-related events\nsignal battle_over_screen_requested(text: String, type: BattleOverPanel.Type)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 15. `/workspace/custom_resources/card.gd` (52 lines)\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name Card\nextends Resource\n\nenum Type {ATTACK, SKILL, POWER}\nenum Target {SELF, SINGLE_ENEMY, ALL_ENEMIES, EVERYONE}\n\n@export_group(\"Card Attributes\")\n@export var id: String\n@export var type: Type\n@export var target: Target\n@export var cost: int\n\n@export_group(\"Card Visuals\")\n@export var icon: Texture\n@export_multiline var tooltip_text: String\n@export var sound: AudioStream\n\n\nfunc is_single_targeted() -> bool:\n\treturn target == Target.SINGLE_ENEMY\n\n\nfunc _get_targets(targets: Array[Node]) -> Array[Node]:\n\tif not targets:\n\t\treturn []\n\t\t\n\tvar tree := targets[0].get_tree()\n\t\n\tmatch target:\n\t\tTarget.SELF:\n\t\t\treturn tree.get_nodes_in_group(\"player\")\n\t\tTarget.ALL_ENEMIES:\n\t\t\treturn tree.get_nodes_in_group(\"enemies\")\n\t\tTarget.EVERYONE:\n\t\t\treturn tree.get_nodes_in_group(\"player\") + tree.get_nodes_in_group(\"enemies\")\n\t\t_:\n\t\t\treturn []\n\n\nfunc play(targets: Array[Node], char_stats: CharacterStats) -> void:\n\tEvents.card_played.emit(self)\n\tchar_stats.mana -= cost\n\t\n\tif is_single_targeted():\n\t\tapply_effects(targets)\n\telse:\n\t\tapply_effects(_get_targets(targets))\n\n\nfunc apply_effects(_targets: Array[Node]) -> void:\n\tpass\n```\n\n---\n\n### 16. `/workspace/scenes/card_target_selector/card_target_selector.gd` (78 lines)\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\nconst ARC_POINTS := 8\n\n@onready var area_2d: Area2D = $Area2D\n@onready var card_arc: Line2D = $CanvasLayer/CardArc\n\nvar current_card: CardUI\nvar targeting := false\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tEvents.card_aim_started.connect(_on_card_aim_started)\n\tEvents.card_aim_ended.connect(_on_card_aim_ended)\n\n\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\tif not targeting:\n\t\treturn\n\n\tarea_2d.position = get_local_mouse_position()\n\tcard_arc.points = _get_points()\n\n\nfunc _get_points() -> Array:\n\tvar points := []\n\tvar start := current_card.global_position\n\tstart.x += (current_card.size.x / 2)\n\tvar target := get_local_mouse_position()\n\tvar distance := (target - start)\n\t\n\tfor i in ARC_POINTS:\n\t\tvar t := (1.0 / ARC_POINTS) * i\n\t\tvar x := start.x + (distance.x / ARC_POINTS) * i\n\t\tvar y := start.y + ease_out_cubic(t) * distance.y\n\t\tpoints.append(Vector2(x, y))\n\t\n\tpoints.append(target)\n\t\n\treturn points\n\n\nfunc ease_out_cubic(number : float) -> float:\n\treturn 1.0 - pow(1.0 - number, 3.0)\n\n\nfunc _on_card_aim_started(card: CardUI) -> void:\n\tif not card.card.is_single_targeted():\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\ttargeting = true\n\tarea_2d.monitoring = true\n\tarea_2d.monitorable = true\n\tcurrent_card = card\n\n\nfunc _on_card_aim_ended(_card: CardUI) -> void:\n\ttargeting = false\n\tcard_arc.clear_points()\n\tarea_2d.position = Vector2.ZERO\n\tarea_2d.monitoring = false\n\tarea_2d.monitorable = false\n\tcurrent_card = null\n\n\nfunc _on_area_2d_area_entered(area: Area2D) -> void:\n\tif not current_card or not targeting:\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tif not current_card.targets.has(area):\n\t\tcurrent_card.targets.append(area)\n\n\nfunc _on_area_2d_area_exited(area: Area2D) -> void:\n\tif not current_card or not targeting:\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tcurrent_card.targets.erase(area)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 17. `/workspace/task_config.json` (3 lines)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Finish the card dragging mechanic for the alternate harness. The provided `res://scenes/main.tscn` harness keeps three `CardUI` instances under `CombatHUD/Slots`, and each card should continue using the existing `CardStateMachine`, `CardBaseState`, `CardClickedState`, and `CardDraggingState` nodes from `res://scenes/card_ui/card_ui.tscn`. In `res://scenes/card_ui/card_state_machine.gd`, initialize every child state, connect each state's `transition_requested` signal, enter the exported `initial_state`, and forward `_input` and `gui_input` to the active state while ignoring transition requests that do not come from the current state. In `res://scenes/card_ui/card_ui.gd`, call `card_state_machine.init(self)` in `_ready()`, forward the existing input callbacks into the state machine, and keep `targets` updated from the `DropPointDetector` area enter/exit callbacks without duplicates. In the card state scripts, make the base state emit `reparent_requested`, reset `DropPointDetector.monitoring` to `false`, and move to the clicked state on left-click, make the clicked state record `original_index`, enable `DropPointDetector.monitoring`, and transition to dragging on mouse motion, make the dragging state reparent the card into the node in the `float_layer` group, follow the mouse, cancel back to base on right-click, and only confirm release after `DRAG_MINIMUM_THRESHOLD := 0.03` has elapsed, and make the released state immediately remove the card when `targets` is not empty but otherwise go back to base on the next input. In `res://scenes/ui/hand.gd`, connect each new card's `reparent_requested` signal and restore cancelled drags back into `Slots` at their recorded index.\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Search Results for Specific Terms\n\n| Term | Locations Found |\n|---|---|\n| `reparent_requested` | `card_ui.gd` line 3 (signal declaration), `task_config.json` (instruction mentions it twice) |\n| `float_layer` | `main.tscn` line 19 (CombatHUD is in the `float_layer` group), `.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg` line 15, `task_config.json` line 2 (instruction) |\n| `DropPointDetector` | `card_ui.tscn` lines 54/58/84/85 (node and signal connections), `card_ui.gd` line 10 (`@onready`), `task_config.json` (instruction) |\n| `targets` | 28 occurrences across `card_ui.gd`, `card.gd`, `card_target_selector.gd`, `card_aiming_state.gd`, `effect.gd`, `block_effect.gd`, `damage_effect.gd`, warrior card scripts, `card_template.gd`, `task_config.json` |\n| `DRAG_MINIMUM_THRESHOLD` | `card_dragging_state.gd` line 3 (`const DRAG_MINIMUM_THRESHOLD := 0.03`), `task_config.json` (instruction) |\n| `CardReleasedState` | `card_ui.tscn` line 77 (node name) |\n| `card_released_state` | `card_ui.tscn` line 8 (resource path `res://scenes/card_ui/card_states/card_released_state.gd`), `.godot/editor/filesystem_cache10` lines 124/130 |\n\n---\n\n## How Everything Relates\n\n**Scene Hierarchy:**\n- `Main` (Node2D) is the root, scripted by `main.gd`\n  - `CommitArea` (Area2D) -- collision layer 2, a 260x88 drop detection zone\n  - `CombatHUD` (CanvasLayer, group=`float_layer`) -- the floating layer for drag operations\n    - `Slots` (HBoxContainer, scripted by `hand.gd`) -- holds all card UIs\n\n**CardUI Scene (instantiated by `hand.gd`):**\n- `CardUI` (Control, scripted by `card_ui.gd`)\n  - `Panel`, `Title`, `State` -- visual elements\n  - `DropPointDetector` (Area2D) -- collision mask 2, detects overlapping drop areas\n  - `CardStateMachine` (Node, scripted by `card_state_machine.gd`)\n    - `CardBaseState`\n    - `CardClickedState`\n    - `CardDraggingState` (contains `DRAG_MINIMUM_THRESHOLD = 0.03`)\n    - `CardReleasedState`\n\n**State Flow (from the task instruction):**\n1. **Base** -- emit `reparent_requested`, set `DropPointDetector.monitoring = false`, transition to Clicked on left-click\n2. **Clicked** -- record `original_index`, enable `DropPointDetector.monitoring`, transition to Dragging on mouse motion\n3. **Dragging** -- reparent into `float_layer` group node, follow mouse, cancel back to Base on right-click, confirm release to Released after `DRAG_MINIMUM_THRESHOLD` seconds\n4. **Released** -- if `targets` not empty, remove card (play); otherwise go back to Base on next input\n\n**`hand.gd`** connects each new card's `reparent_requested` signal and should restore cancelled drags back into `Slots` at their `original_index`.\n\nThere is **no** `drop_point_detector.gd` file in the project -- `DropPointDetector` is just an `Area2D` node in the scene with no separate script. All drop detection is handled via signal connections in `card_ui.tscn` routed to `_on_drop_point_detector_area_entered` and `_on_drop_point_detector_area_exited` in `card_ui.gd` (both currently empty stubs).\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId